From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: domicile CI <ci@domicile.invalid>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] domicile: a webview's page asks the shell for a device

WebHID, WebUSB and Web Serial each ask for a device through
chrome::ShowDeviceChooserDialog, a bubble anchored to a browser window.
A <webview> guest has no browser window, so the bubble never showed
and the page was given no device. A Ledger wallet's extension could not
connect.

//chrome/browser/domicile sets an override that asks the shell instead
(domicile_device_chooser.h). This patch carries the parts in files
Chromium owns:

- `browser_dialogs.{h,cc}`: SetDeviceChooserOverride and its getter.
- `chooser_bubble_ui.cc`: ShowDeviceChooserDialog uses the override
  when one is set.
- Three lists, so that `DomicileDeviceRequestEvent`, the event a
  `<webview>` dispatches for the shell to answer, and `DomicileDevice`,
  the dictionary it lists devices in, are compiled and reach the page,
  as patch 0103 does for permission requests.

Verified: not built. This repository cannot build Chromium; the engine
job builds it on `crux`.
